1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:07,400
Stainless steel maintenance access — at a data centre on Sunview Drive.

2
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:12,330
Handrails and access cat-ladder, mounted on the side of data containers.

3
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:16,150
The challenge? No welding allowed on the container.

4
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:20,200
So every base plate is bolted to the existing steel channel.

5
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:29,950
SS304-grade handrails, engineered to Singapore Standards and Professional Engineer approved for load calculation.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,050
The cat-ladder is secured safe for the user with a fall-arrestor system —

7
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:40,530
using a certified self-retracting lifeline mounted on a stainless steel support frame.

8
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:46,200
This frame structure is fixed to the existing structure. No welds. Full strength.

9
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:50,120
The result: safe, Professional Engineer certified maintenance access.

10
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:56,800
By Ezzogenics. Engineered, bolted, safe.
